Nethack should allow some way for characters to make their own traps.
I seem to remember that urogue simply added a trap command with some
probability of failure.  But that was too easy, because you could just
keep trying and eventually you would be able to make the trap.

Here's what may be a better solution:  wands aimed at the ground (>)
create a trap.  These traps can either be permanent or of a finite
duration.  Whether the wand is blessed/uncursed/cursed makes a
difference:

	blessed		character always escapes the trap
	uncursed	trap takes effect only after character steps
				off of it
	cursed		trap takes effect immediately (wile character
			is still standing on it after zapping)

Most wands create a trap which behaves just like the wand, but a few
are different.  Below is, I think, a complete list of wands and the
traps they would make:

	WAND			TRAP
	magic missile		arrow/dart (permanent)
	fire			fire (perm)
	sleep			sleep gas (perm)
	cold			cold (perm)
	death			death (perm)
	lightning		lightning (perm)
	slow monster		slow monster (perm)
	speed monster		speed monster (perm)
	polymorph		polymorph (once on character)
	digging			trapdoor (perm)
				(digs in one turn, unlike pick-axe)
	undead turning		undead won't step on it (perm)
	cancellation		anit-magic field (perm)
				(works on monsters, too)
	create monster		create monster (no. of charges on
				wand)
	secret door detection	shows all secret doors on level (once)
	make invisible		make invisible (perm)
	nothing			nothing; magic trap if cursed (perm)
	probing			identify random pack items (once)
				or
				act like monster/object/gold detection
				(perm)
	opening			pack opens, random items fall out,
				with chance of potions breeaking
				(perm)
	locking			paralysis? (perm)
	wishing			a djinni appears, may not be friendly
				(once)
	striking		landmine (once)
	teleportation		teleporter (perm)
				level teleporter if cursed (once on
				character)
	light			blinds (perm)

So how about it for 3.1?

